  "source_id": "county-055",
  "text": "Elections | County of Lincoln, NC - Official Website\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account\n- Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nGovernment\nResidents\nVisitors\nBusiness\nSearch\nCampaign Finance\nOpen Candidate Committees\n2026 Election Information\nElection Events\nElection Results\nStaff\nVoting\nAbsentee Voting\nHandicapped and Curbside Voting\nPolling Locations\nVoter Registration\nVoting Election Day\nVote in Honor of a Veteran\nHome\nGovernment\nDepartments\nElections\nElections\nOVERVIEW\nThe goal of the Board of Elections is to provide the citizens of the county with the best possible services, and to conduct fair, honest and impartial elections in an efficient and economical manner.\nThe Board of Election Office is charged with the overall responsibility of administering the election process and campaign finance disclosures for all elections held in Lincoln County.\nELECTION NOTICE\n2026 General Election Notice\nPUBLIC NOTICE\nUpcoming Election: Sample Ballots\nCity of Lincolnton Residents\nLincoln County Residents\nPUBLIC NOTICE\nLincoln County Board of Elections will conduct Logic and Accuracy testing on voting equipment on September 9th, 10th, and 14th 8:30AM - until.\nPUBLIC NOTICE\nLincoln County Board of Elections Absentee meeting schedule.\nClick here for link.\nPUBLIC NOTICE\nEarly Voting Schedule for General Election.\nClick here for the link\n.\nPUBLIC NOTICE\nOfficial Primary Election Results.\nClick here for the link\n.\nPUBLIC NOTICE\nList of 2026 General Election Candidates.\nClick here for the link\n.\nPUBLIC NOTICE\nLincoln County Candidate Filing has ended. Click the link for the final list of candidates.\nClick here for a pdf\n.\nVOTER STATISTICS BY PRECINCT\nIncludes all Active and Inactive voters sorted by precinct as of October 2nd, 2026.\nClick here for a PDF\n.\nPUBLIC NOTICE\nUpcoming 2026 Election Information.\nClick here for PDF\n.\nPUBLIC NOTICE - Photo ID\nFor more information, go to\nVoter ID\non the State Board of Elections website. Also see\nInfosheet: Voter Photo ID Requirements\n. And\nFAQ: Voter ID\n.\nHOW TO REGISTER TO VOTE IN NORTH CAROLINA\nClick here to watch the video\nPUBLIC NOTICE - Public Records Request\nPublic Records Request must be made in writing and sent to the Elections Office. Please allow up to 7 days for requests to be processed. Requests will not be processed until payment is received.\nPublic Records Request Form\nPUBLIC NOTICE - 2021 Lincoln County School Board Map\nGIS Download Page\nPUBLIC NOTICE - Board Meeting Policy\nThe Lincoln County Board of Elections has adopted a policy on speaking at all board meetings.\nClick here for a pdf of the policy\nEarly Voting and Election Official Application\nClick here for the application.\nElection Complaint Form\nClick here for the PDF form\n.\nVOTE IN HONOR OF A VETERAN\nThe Vote in Honor of a Veteran Program provides North Carolinians with an opportunity to pay tribute to those who have served this country in the Armed Forces. Any voter can honor a veteran on any Election Day by requesting a pin. Pins are provided for free by the State Board of Elections. Each pin can be personalized with the name of the veteran a voter wishes to honor.\nClick here to order pin\nLincoln County Board of Elections Members 2025-2027\nJosh Gantt Chairman\nCharles Newman Secretary\nDon Wise Member\nBrian Crisson Member\nDean Black Member\nThe State Board of Elections website has archived election results on its website. The link to the website is\nhttp://www.ncsbe.gov\n.\nContact Us\nBradley Putnam\nDirector\nEmail\nBoard of Elections\nPhysical Address\nView Map\n451 Salem Church Rd.\nLincolnton\n,\nNC\n28092\n451 Salem Church Rd. Lincolnton NC 28092\nDirections\nPhone:\n(704) 736-8480\nFax: (704) 736-8804\nHours\n8\nam\nto 5\npm\nMonday through Friday\nDirectory\nAgendas\n& Minutes\nOnline\nPayments\nEmployment\nOnline\nServices\nGIS & Maps\nAdoptable Pets\nContact Us\nLincoln County Government\n353 N. Generals Blvd.\nLincolnton, NC 28092\nPO Box 738, Lincolnton, NC 28093-0738\nWebsite Sign In\nQuick Links\nDepartments\nCommunity Resources\nAfter Hours Essential Service Phone Numbers\nAdoptable Pets from Animal Services\nApply for a Passport\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nSite Links\nHome\nSite Map\nContact Us\nAccessibility\nCopyright Notices\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by\nCivicPlus\u00ae\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nArrow Left\nArrow Right\n[]\nSlideshow Left Arrow\nSlideshow Right Arrow",
